        "title": "Spacecraft reaches Mercury on second-ever mission to enter its orbit",
        "source": "The Guardian - Science",
        "source_id": "guardian_science",
        "category": "culture",
        "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/nov/20/spacecraft-mercury-second-ever-mission-orbit-bepicolombo",
        "published_at": "2026-11-20T00:01:15",
        "level": "C2",
        "slot_level": "C2",
        "source_level": "C1",
        "word_count": 545,
        "duration_sec": null,
        "body_text": "After a voyage of more than eight years and 6bn miles, a joint European-Japanese space mission has arrived at Mercury and is preparing to swing into orbit around the tiny, barely explored world.",
        "audio_url": null,
        "description": null,
        "license": "proprietary",
        "attribution": null,
        "truncated": true,
        "guid_hash": "dfdf9519a4809038ea2f58b7325e8c30e345bae1",
        "summary": "BepiColombo double probe will map planet’s surface and study its interior to shed light on its unusually large core After a voyage of more than eight years and 6bn miles, a joint European-Japanese space mission has arrived at Mercury and is preparing to swing into orbit around the tiny, barely explored world. The BepiColombo mission will become only the second in history to circle the first rock from the sun and the smallest planet in the solar system when flight controllers fire the spacecraft’s thrusters on Saturday and send it into orbit.",
